<!--
  A double accumulator is copied from nonvolatile XMM6 to return register XMM0
  before a locked-void MSVC cookie checker. The cookie slot is carried through a
  loop, and the checker's failure tail contains a nested call before int 0x29,
  so the generic body probe cannot justify preservation. The exact
  `(cookie ^ SP) ^ SP` marker can. The final function is a negative control: its
  void callee writes XMM0 and then reaches a nested call, so the incomplete
  production probe must retain that recovered write and veto preservation.

  wide_exact_caller loads both lanes of XMM0 before a proven cookie call. Its
  low 8-byte lane is the Win64 logical return storage and survives; the upper
  lane is scratch and must remain killed. Reading the upper lane after the call
  makes a whole-register downgrade observable as the wrong constant 3.5.
-->
